{
 "_id": "api-calls-fixture",
 "_comment": "WTF-533: API Connector calls lowered to Req clients, all data invented (host api.example.test, stubbed in test/support/target/phoenix/api_calls_behavior.exs; never a real API). An API (Example, key in a header) with two calls: Get item (GET, a URL parameter, a query parameter, a private header; returns an Item) and Post note (POST JSON with a private body parameter, errors included in the response). A backend workflow fetches an item and returns its name; page buttons fetch an item and post a note, showing the result in a label. A catalog page reads data calls (WTF-533, slice 2): List items (GET, a list of rows filtered by an input's value) feeds a repeating group and a group's first row; Get price is called in the repeating group's cells, per cell (residue) and with a fixed value (once); Get status, whose private header the tests never set, shows as empty with a developer marker.",
 "user_types": {
  "user": {
   "display": "User",
   "fields": {
    "email": {
     "display": "email",
     "value": "text"
    }
   }
  },
  "note": {
   "display": "Note",
   "fields": {
    "title_text": {
     "display": "Title",
     "value": "text"
    }
   }
  }
 },
